// Distributed schedule for example 27-bin-fmin (TASK-0343.02).
//
// The FLOAT MIN-combine sibling of 26-bin-min/distributed. Mirrors it
// EXACTLY (i-band partition, whole-array replicate, host element-wise
// combine) — the load-bearing difference is the scalar TYPE (f32 vs
// i32) and so its identity: `bin_fmin` declares `combine=min`, whose
// float identity is `f32::INFINITY`. Every per-worker partial AND the
// host `result` MUST pre-init to `f32::INFINITY` (not 0.0), and the
// host emits `result[_k] = result[_k].min(_tmp[_k])` (Rust f32::min,
// method form).
//
// Shape:
//   host    — owns I/O (load_key / load_val / save_output).
//   w0..w3  — each compute worker owns one i-band of the inputs and
//             min-folds it into a private FULL-width `result` (whole-
//             array replicate, pre-init f32::INFINITY). The compiler
//             partitions the outer `i` loop across the four workers via
//             partition=workers.
//
// Cross-worker edges:
//   key     host -> { w0..w3 }   (host loads, workers consume)
//   val     host -> { w0..w3 }   (host loads, workers consume)
//   result  { w0..w3 } -> host   (workers produce, host MIN-combines)
//
// Why the combine is sound: `min` is associative + commutative for the
// distinct finite positive values this fixture commits to, and the
// i-band partition is a DISJOINT cover of the inputs — each input is
// min-folded into its bin exactly once, in exactly one worker's partial.
// A worker whose band contains no `key==b` keeps `result[b] ==
// f32::INFINITY` (the identity), so the host `min(f32::INFINITY, ...)`
// correctly ignores it. The element-wise min of the 4 full partials
// equals the global per-bin minimum, independent of worker arrival
// order => bit-identical across all 7 tier-1 backends (PRD §10.1).
//
// All `sync` (the default transfer mode). `partition=workers` is the
// partition policy for the outer `i` loop — the same shape examples
// 03-reduction / 08-histogram / 25-bin-parity / 26-bin-min use.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // I/O on host.
    place load_key    on host;
    place load_val    on host;
    place save_output on host;

    // The pure step kernel distributed across compute workers.
    place bin_fmin on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Outer loop is the partition axis; one slice per compute worker.
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // Cross-worker data — one transfer per data symbol that crosses.
    transfer key    : sync;
    transfer val    : sync;
    transfer result : sync;
}
